{
  "_comment": "Format profiles read by beatmap_lint.py. `mix` = allowed share of RUNTIME by BASE layer (overlays do not count). beat_seconds = band for one beat's spoken length. Edit here, never in code. hyperframes_workflow = the HyperFrames workflow that builds the code layer (host-broll: the overlay track only; the base is explainer-reel-skill). host_covers_full_vo = the avatar call is billed for the whole voice-over (the host is the clock), so the linter prices host seconds on total runtime, not on host beats only. `wps` is a PRIOR in speech units per second (words, or characters for unsegmented scripts); it is replaced by a measured rate (scripts/speech_rate.py) and the linter treats duration checks as warnings until it is. `read` = the reference files (stems under references/) to read for this format beyond the always-read set in SKILL.md; `needs_punchline` and `punchline_max_seconds` are house heuristics for comedy, editable; `allow_repeat_treatment` permits three identical layer+device beats in a row (shot and reverse shot in dialogue). `looks` lists the identities the format's doc allows (empty = any); style_lock.py pick respects it.",
